## Introduction

Integrating a payment terminal with Centrapay APIs allows merchants to accept payment via any Centrapay-enabled apps using the payment terminals they already have, without installing additional hardware.

## Payment Flow

- [QR Code Flow](/guides/merchant-integration-qr-code-flow): the terminal displays a QR code for the patron to scan with their Centrapay app.

## Interface Guidelines

Use the [Centrapay Logos](/guides/centrapay-logos) when building the UI for Centrapay payments.

### Payment Option

Always display **Centrapay** as a payment option. Choose the Centrapay logo format that best suits the screen size, and present it as a payment option button. Use the [Centrapay brand orange](/guides/centrapay-logos#brand-colour) wherever possible.

![Two payment terminals showing the Centrapay logo on the payment screen](/guideline/guideline-01.png)

### QR Code

The payment QR code screen must display the **Centrapay logo**, for example above or below the QR code, or in the centre of the QR code. The copy can be "**Scan to pay**" or "**Scan to pay with Centrapay**".

![Two payment terminals showing a Centrapay QR code with the Centrapay logo and Scan to pay copy](/guideline/guideline-02.png)
